# Line endings.
#
# `scripts/py.sh` is run as `bash py.sh ...` and is pure POSIX sh. A Windows
# checkout that converted it to CRLF would break it in the way that is hardest
# to read: bash treats the trailing \r as part of the last word on the line, so
# `exit 0` becomes `exit 0\r` and every quoted path grows an invisible
# character. Pin every shell script to LF on every platform, whatever the
# clone's core.autocrlf says.
* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
